    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.basicr\n\n### Description\n\nHJKL navigation is used in a couple of spots in basics, as well as in move. However, in move, they can be customized but can't in basics. This would be a very nice feature to have for people who use other keys to move (alternate layout users, for example). ",
