        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Yes, very sorry, I'm requesting the window navigation and insert mode cursor movements be configurable like the line and selection movement is. For my use case I'd like HNEI to match the colemak layout, but I'm sure others would have other use cases.\r\n\r\nI see. Thanks for clarification.\r\n\r\n'mini.basics' is initially designed to provide some \"easy to opt-in\" set of options/mappings/autocommands. Having them configurable will make the interface harder.\r\n\r\nThe proposed way of customizing the provided functionality is to read source code and adapt to your need. This will really be beneficial in long term. Here are [the window navigation mappings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/basics.lua#L637) and here are [the \"move with alt\"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/basics.lua#L653) command to make mappings (`map` is essentially a `vim.keymap.set` function). To customize them, don't enable those config parts during `require('mini.basics').setup()` and add code with your own mapped keys.\r\n\r\nClosing this, as another approach is recommended to customize 'mini.basics'.",
            "created_at": "2023-05-08T13:45:08Z",
